a white former police officer faces a  murder charge this morning for shooting  a black woman inside her Texas home Erin  Dean posted bond overnight following his  arrest late yesterday he resigned  earlier in the day before he could be  fired from the Fort Worth Police  Department Dean shot 28 year old Tatyana  Jefferson as he was responding to a  neighbor's call for a wellness check  Omar Villafranca is outside Fort Worth  police headquarters Omar good morning  how are the victim's family reacting to  this murder charge  the family is relieved that the officer  was arrested and charged with murder but  they're quick to say that this is not  just about the officer but the way the  Fort Worth police department trains  their officers and we talked to a former  Fort Worth cop who agrees and says the  department needs to change as a black  female former police officer I'm afraid  when I get stopped former Fort Worth  police officer LaRhonda Young says she  doesn't trust the department's officers  and she feels  twenty-eight-year-old that Tatiana  Jefferson's death represents a clear  breach of protocol officers are shooting  before assessing situations if that  officer had simply knocked on the door  that young lady would be alive today  officer Aaron Dean resigned yesterday  body cam footage shows the moment he  shot and killed Jefferson in her home on  Saturday the video shows Dean who's now  charged with murder never identified  himself as a police officer Clark he was  responding to a 2:00 a.m. wellness call  from Jefferson's neighbor but interim  Police Chief Ed Krause said it may not  have been clear there was no emergency  if they thought they had something more  criminal Jefferson's siblings Ashley in  a Darius car say it's a sign the  department has to change what their  attorney called a brutal culture of  policing no gun should even been out  there was no threat when you heard the  gunshot came through a window what was  your response  that's drive-by material Police Chief  Krause agrees there's no excuse for  Dean's actions what can you tell members  of the community who have told us  incidents like this are why'd they do  not trust Fort Worth police I tell them  and get it we're trying to ensure that  they act and react for the servant's  heart instead of a warrior's heart Dean  was charged with murder but the  investigation will not stop there in  fact Fort Worth city officials have  handed over a preliminary case to the  FBI to look into possible civil rights  violations we are expecting an update on  the criminal case later on this morning  Anthony such an upsetting story Omar  thank you
 

